From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shipwright <shipwright@invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:06:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Report whether the host presents Apple's Device ID

AirPods enable hearing aid, customised transparency, loud sound
reduction and multi-device use only for hosts whose Device ID (DID
profile) carries Apple's Bluetooth SIG company identifier, 0x004C.
BlueZ sets the Device ID from "DeviceID" in main.conf and reports it as
org.bluez.Adapter1.Modalias ("bluetooth:v004Cp0000d0000").

- HostDeviceId tracks the selected adapter's Modalias (read on selection
  in the same GetAll as Powered, where its absence means no Device ID is
  configured; followed through PropertiesChanged; cleared when the
  adapter goes) and says whether it is Apple's. It is published under
  the same lock as Powered, so a removed adapter's value is never
  published after its removal.
- MAGICPODS_HOST_DEVICE_ID overrides it with a modalias string.
- New method GetHostDevice: {"hostdevice": {"appleDeviceId": bool,
  "modalias": string}}, also part of GetAll and broadcast when
  appleDeviceId changes. It is a separate object so that existing
  "defaultbluetooth" frames do not change.

Background: LibrePods (https://github.com/librepods-org/librepods,
README "VendorID Spoofing", linux/README.md "Hearing Aid") documents
which AirPods features depend on the host's Device ID.
